00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:06,000
The Seven Five, also known as Seven Five Precinct, is a 2014 documentary directed by Tiller
Russell, and produced by Eli Holzman, Aaron Saidman, and Sheldon Yellen.

7
00:59:30,000 --> 00:59:36,000
The film looks at police corruption in the 75th Precinct of the
New York Police Department during the 1980s.

8
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
The documentary focuses on Michael Dowd and Kenneth Eurell, both corrupt New York City police officers, who were
arrested in 1992, leading to one of the largest police corruption scandals in New York City history.

9
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
The documentary uses footage from the Mollen Commission investigation in 1992 and also
provides in-depth commentary from Dowd, Ken Eurell, and Adam Diaz, among others.

10
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
The documentary premiered at DOC NYC November 14, 2014.

11
01:33:30,000 --> 01:33:36,000
The film explores themes of new york city,
corruption, mobster, mafia, police corruption.
